# 4 entries, one genuinely distinct fact per line.
malungkot | definition | Malungkot means sad or sorrowful, and it is the ordinary Tagalog word for feeling low, for missing someone and for grief at a loss. It is closer to a sustained mood than to a single moment, so a person who has been sad for days is malungkot, while a brief reaction to something is more likely magdamdam or a specific word. The related distinction worth learning is between feeling sad about yourself and feeling sorry for someone else, which English also keeps apart: malungkot is the first, while the word for pity or compassion covers the second, and a learner who uses malungkot for a third party is understood to be talking about themselves. A parallel form uses a prefix for the condition and a different one for the action of consoling, and the pair of words for the person consoling and the person consoled is a common exam item. | sad, sorrow, grief, feeling, mood, missing, pity | anong meaning ng malungkot, malungkot meaning, ano ang maglungkot | dugtong | malungkot
